{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-57415",
  "enisaUuid": "e4ddacec-8f7b-3be1-a519-bf51f7646fcb",
  "description": "An authorization bypass vulnerability in LXD allows an authenticated attacker to bypass target project security restrictions during cross-project instance migrations. When moving an instance cross-project to a different cluster member via POST /1.0/instances/{name} with migration: true, project: <target>, and target: <member>, the destination node skips all project restriction checks because the request arrives as an internal cluster notification. An attacker can exploit this to introduce disallowed instance configurations into a restricted project.",
